NAME
====

**wattle-test** - run the tests of a project

SYNOPSIS
========

**wattle test** [_options_]

DESCRIPTION
===========

**wattle test** runs each file ending in ``.wattle`` under `./test/` in the
current directory. Each file runs in a separate process. **t** is a synonym
for ***test***.

The output begins with ``seed:`` and the seed used to determine the test
order. Each file then has a summary line with a result mark, its path and
the counts of tests and assertions. Output from a failed file is printed
below its summary, with a border that is red when colour is enabled. Output
from a successful file is not printed.

The final summary gives the number of files and tests and lists the files
that failed. The exit status is 1 if any file failed or no file was run.

Test files that use the Gum test module, `gum/test.wattle`, read the dynamic
bindings set by **-t**, **-T** and **--seed**. These options select tests
within a file and control their order.

OPTIONS
=======

- **-f**, **--file** _path_:
  Run only the test file whose path ends with _path_, which is relative to
  `./test/`. This option can be repeated. It is not compatible with **-F**.

- **-F**, **--no-file** _path_:
  Skips the test file whose path ends with _path_, relative to `./test/`.
  This option can be repeated. It is not compatible with **-f**.

- **-t**, **--test** _name_:
  Add _name_ to the dynamic binding ``:test/tests`` in each test file. It can
  be repeated. It is not compatible with **-T**.

- **-T**, **--no-test** _name_:
  Add _name_ to the dynamic binding ``:test/skips`` in each test file. It can
  be repeated. It is not compatible with **-t**.

- **--seed** _seed_:
  Use the integer _seed_ to seed the generator that shuffles the test files.
  The command also sets the dynamic binding ``:test/seed``, which Gum test
  files use to shuffle their tests. Without **--seed**, the seed is taken
  from the clock, so the order varies between runs. The same seed gives the
  same order.

- **-b**, **--bail**:
  Stop after the first test file that fails.

- **-e**, **--lint-error** _level_, **-w**, **--lint-warn** _level_:
  Set the lint levels of each test file. They take the same values as for
  **wattle** ***check***.

EXAMPLES
========

Run the tests in `./test/`, skipping one file:

````
$ wattle test --no-file slow.wattle
````

SEE ALSO
========

`wattle(1)`, `wattle-check(1)`
